  "user_request_original": "Design a planar multilayer stack with air incidence on an aluminum substrate. Stack sequence from air to substrate: HfO2 / Cr (Rakic-LD) / SiO2 (Lemarchand) / HfO2 / Cr (Rakic-LD) / SiO2 (Lemarchand) / HfO2 / Cr (Rakic-LD) / SiO2 (Lemarchand) / HfO2 / SiO2 (Lemarchand), terminating at aluminum substrate. Total layer count is 13 (3 Cr (Rakic-LD) + 10 dielectric + Al (Rakic-LD) substrate not counted as film layer). Optimize the thickness of each chromium layer independently and each dielectric layer thickness independently. Wavelength range 400-2000 nm. Target: maximize absorptance in 400-700 nm through distributed absorption, maximize reflectance in 700-2000 nm. Normal incidence, unpolarized light.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize the thickness of each finite layer in an 11-layer planar stack (HfO2/Cr/SiO2 repeated four times plus final HfO2/SiO2) on an aluminum substrate under normal unpolarized incidence across 400-2000 nm. Maximize average absorptance in 400-700 nm and maximize average reflectance in 700-2000 nm.",
